    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "e3a9cb5f956bdaa19e04a1d0f3f8f730",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"decay-width\">Decay width</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Write <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(M=m_H||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(r=m^2/M^2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta=\\sqrt{1-4r}||)</marimo-tex>. The shared two-body\nphase-space measure is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d\\Phi_2/d\\Omega=\\beta/(32\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex> and the rest-frame\ndecay flux is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(2M||)</marimo-tex>. Integrating over solid angle gives\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\Gamma=S\\beta\\sum|\\mathcal M|^2/(16\\pi M)||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The identical-particle factor is <strong><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(S=1/2!||)</marimo-tex> for <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(ZZ||)</marimo-tex></strong> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(S=1||)</marimo-tex> for the\ndistinct <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(W^-W^+||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(f\\bar f||)</marimo-tex> final states. It is applied once, to the\nphase-space integral. For the <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(ZZ||)</marimo-tex> comparison we use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(m_W=m_Z\\cos\\theta_W||)</marimo-tex>;\nfor fermions we identify the Yukawa mass with the kinematic mass at tree level.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The gallery widths, with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\alpha=e^2/(4\\pi)||)</marimo-tex>, are</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\Gamma_{f\\bar f}=\\frac{N_c\\alpha M m_f^2}{8m_W^2\\sin^2\\theta_W}\\beta^3,||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\Gamma_{WW}=\\frac{\\alpha M^3}{16m_W^2\\sin^2\\theta_W}\n  \\beta(1-4r+12r^2),\\qquad\n  \\Gamma_{ZZ}=\\frac{\\alpha M^3}{32m_W^2\\sin^2\\theta_W}\n  \\beta(1-4r+12r^2).||)</marimo-tex>$\nHere <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N_c=1||)</marimo-tex> for leptons and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(3||)</marimo-tex> for quarks; use the selected final-particle\nmass in <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(r||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
